Subject: [PATCH 08/14] fix(trace): name the pixel grid that px settings count
 on (ADR-396)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Trace decodes large images at most 2048 px on a side, and Remove ink
specks, Ignore Less Than, Minimum line and Centerline's gap all count
pixels of that decoded grid. The dialog header shows the imported image's
own size, so on a 4096 px image a 12 px² speck setting silently meant 48
source px². When the decoded grid differs from the image size, the
settings panel now says so under Refine detail, for example "Tracing at
2048 × 1536 px; pixel settings use this grid." The size comes from the
latest finished preview of the same image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
